---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Code from "@/components/Code.astro";
const snippet0 = `from power_pptx import Presentation

prs = Presentation("deck.pptx")
for slide in prs.slides:
    report = slide.lint()
    for issue in report.issues:
        print(issue.severity.value, issue)`;

const snippet1 = `report = slide.lint()
report.auto_fix()          # mutates: nudges OffSlide shapes back inside

# One call instead of lint → fix → re-lint
slide.tidy()`;

const snippet2 = `from power_pptx.compose import from_spec

prs = from_spec({
    "slides": [{"layout": "title", "title": "Q4 Review"}],
    "lint": "raise",                  # raise | warn | off
})`;

const snippet3 = `from power_pptx import audit

report = audit(prs)
print(report.markdown())`;

---

<DocsLayout
  title="Lint & Audit"
  description="slide.lint(), issue types and severities, auto_fix, tidy(), the from_spec lint hook, and whole-deck audit()."
>
  <p class="lead">
    The layout linter is the last line of defence in the space-aware stack: it measures the slide
    and reports anything that would look broken in PowerPoint.
  </p>

  <h2 id="lint">slide.lint()</h2>
  <Code code={snippet0} />

  <h2 id="issues">Issue types</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Type</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Default severity</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>TextOverflow</code></td><td>Estimated text extent exceeds its frame (Pillow metrics)</td><td>warning</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>OffSlide</code></td><td>Shape extends past the slide bounds</td><td>error</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ShapeCollision</code></td><td>Unintentional overlap between shapes</td><td>warning</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="autofix">auto_fix and tidy</h2>
  <Code code={snippet1} />
  <p>
    <code>TextOverflow</code> is reported but <strong>not</strong> auto-fixed — use
    <code>tf.fit_text(...)</code> or <code>auto_size = TEXT_TO_FIT_SHAPE</code> for that.
  </p>

  <h2 id="from-spec">The from_spec lint gate</h2>
  <Code code={snippet2} />

  <h2 id="audit">Whole-deck audit</h2>
  <Code code={snippet3} />
  <p>The audit aggregates, per deck:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>lint issues across every slide</li>
    <li>broken or missing pictures</li>
    <li>empty slides</li>
    <li>uncommon-font warnings (fonts recipients are unlikely to have)</li>
    <li>oversized-picture warnings (bloat)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <code>AuditReport.markdown()</code> formats the lot for a chat reply or CI log.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
